<title>INDIA: India forex reserves ease to $22.90 bln on Oct 4.</title>
<headline>India forex reserves ease to $22.90 bln on Oct 4.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's foreign exchange reserves eased to $22.90 billion on October 4, 1996, from $22.95 billion the previous week, the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said on Monday in its weekly statistical supplement.</p>
<p>	 FOREIGN EXCHANGE RESERVES (in million U.S. dollars)</p>
<p>					  Oct 4	 Sept 27     Oct 6</p>
<p>					    1996	  1996	   1995</p>
<p>    Foreign currency assets     18,474	18,434	 18,959</p>
<p>    Gold				 4,410	 4,455	  4,405</p>
<p>    SDRs				    18	    57		8</p>
<p>    Total			     22,902	22,946	 23,372</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
